{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q106365096","formula":"C₁₇H₆Br₅N₃","hill":"C17H6Br5N3","elements":["H","C","N","Br"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":6.0,"N":3.0,"Br":5.0},"names":{"en":"Aetokthonotoxin"},"descriptions":{"en":"Aetokthonotoxin (AETX), colloquially known as eagle-killer toxin, is a chemical compound that was identified in 2021 as the cyanobacterial neurotoxin causing vacuolar myelinopathy (VM) in eagles in North America. As the biosynthesis of aetokthonotoxin depends on the availability of bromide ions in freshwater systems and requires an interplay between the toxin-producing cyanobacterium Aetokthonos hydrillicola and the host plant it requires to live (Hydrilla verticillata), it took more than 25 years to identify aetokthonotoxin as the VM-inducing toxin after the disease has first been diagnosed in bald eagles in 1994."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":155818808,"mass":651.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC2=C(C=C1Br)C(=C(N2C3=C(C4=C(N3)C(=CC(=C4)Br)Br)C#N)Br)Br","inchikey":"JXJDQKCOJBAPQM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5,7-dibromo-2-(2,3,5-tribromoindol-1-yl)-1H-indole-3-carbonitrile","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"155818808","atoms":31,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.905,"y":-0.472,"z":2.574,"el":"C"},{"x":1.804,"y":-0.41,"z":1.714,"el":"C"},{"x":2.024,"y":-0.147,"z":0.345,"el":"C"},{"x":3.323,"y":-0.002,"z":-0.161,"el":"C"},{"x":4.42,"y":-0.067,"z":0.728,"el":"C"},{"x":4.193,"y":-0.296,"z":2.086,"el":"C"},{"x":5.663,"y":-0.386,"z":3.273,"el":"Br"},{"x":3.195,"y":0.193,"z":-1.555,"el":"C"},{"x":1.862,"y":0.185,"z":-1.88,"el":"C"},{"x":1.128,"y":-0.053,"z":-0.731,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.267,"y":-0.122,"z":-0.619,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.199,"y":-0.782,"z":-1.398,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.491,"y":-0.48,"z":-0.865,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.299,"y":0.34,"z":0.249,"el